WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:10.477
Mathilde One only has to say
the word "English,"

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:15.715
and they come running like
sick black dogs at low tide.

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:21.521
Captain, I heard about
your selfless heroics

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:24.457
with the Iroquois and the
tragedy with the priests.

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:31.798
Well, I suppose there's
nothing more that needs

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:32.931
to be said on the subject.

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:35.235
Silence will suffice then.

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:42.574
Good day.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:49.149
[bell jingling]

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:53.519
Might I have a word, Mathilde?

00:00:56.156 --> 00:00:57.857
Perhaps the kitchen is best.

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:58.691
Of course.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:10.703
I wish to make
you a proposition.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.006
Go on.

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:14.841
I should like to make
use of your stables.

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:17.410
I have an excess of
barrels, trade having slowed

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:19.012
due to the recent unrest.

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:21.581
I am prepared to
pay you handsomely.

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:28.521
You can store
them free of charge.

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:29.823
[pats]

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:31.124
No.

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:32.692
I insist I will pay.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.060
Oh, yes.

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:37.196
A few coins, but that is not
the only reason you are here.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.202
It is.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.971
Oh, and it is a shame,
because there is a greater deal

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:48.708
to be made besides storing
a few barrels in my stables

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:50.076
for some coins.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:52.445
Well, only a fool would refuse
to entertain a greater deal.

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:55.048
Go on.

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:57.083
Go on, [inaudible].

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:57.884
Bye.

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:02.722
You wish to restore your
standing in this town.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:03.756
Am I right?

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:04.958
I shall recover my good name.

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:07.227
Barrels and
trade do not remove

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.596
the stain of your English name.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:10.630
They have before.

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:13.766
Those times are gone.

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.435
You overstepped, Mr. Cooke.

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:19.672
Only a stubborn man would
walk upon a frozen lake

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:21.608
when the sun is shining.

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:23.142
We can help each other.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:26.446
How is that?

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:31.184
I believe Delphine
has caught your eye.

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:38.157
I don't know what
you're talking about.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.993
Come now, Mr. Cooke.

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:41.694
I have seen it with my own eyes.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:44.297
There is no shame in
looking upon her beauty.

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:46.165
It is there for all to see.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:49.335
Now, then, it would
be prudent for you

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:51.103
to make a match with her.

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:56.843
And in return, you will
help me expand the inn.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:03:02.415
Mathilde, I came here merely
to store excess barrels.

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:05.418
And if you agree
to my terms, you

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:07.220
will leave with a French wife.

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:12.559
Right.

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:16.162
Then we shall agree to the
storage of the barrels.

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:18.865
Think on it if
you must, but you

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:20.132
will come to the same place.

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:21.200
[creaking]

